 section('formula','How is a salary increase calculated?',`<div class="formula-grid"><div class="formula-card"><h3>Percentage change</h3><div class="formula">(new pay − current pay) ÷ current pay × 100</div><p class="example">($66,000 − $60,000) ÷ $60,000 × 100 = 10%</p></div><div class="formula-card"><h3>Dollar change</h3><div class="formula">New pay − current pay = annual change</div><p class="example">$66,000 − $60,000 = $6,000 per year</p><p>Monthly, weekly, and hourly changes are just the annual change divided by 12, by 52, and by your scheduled annual hours.</p></div></div>`)
